                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "The seven built-ins, a recent plugin shelf, and Browse all. A plugin chip carries its format as the second line \u2014 the machine fact under the name \u2014 which is also what keeps the cell at the shared two-line height. A name too long for one line truncates; it never wraps, because the grid\u2019s label is single-line. 746 wide, not 744: four 166px columns need 694, plus 25 padding either side and the 1px border each side. Zero slack \u2014 a future padding tweak would silently halve the column count. Mid-scan the count row reads \u201cLooking for plugins\u2026\u201d: a count of zero mid-scan is not a fact about the machine."
              }
            ],
